WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.492 --> 00:00:17.976
"Wow!" Raff thought. "That's amazing.

2
00:00:17.977 --> 00:00:21.348
Two of the kid heroes are coming to Stone Wall!"

3
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.690
His sister had just finished telling him and Loro exactly what Zann and Perda had said.

4
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.726
As the spy fly buzzed away, Zella looked ready to faint from excitement.

5
00:00:31.727 --> 00:00:34.804
"This is incredible!" she said.

6
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:40.767
"Zann and Perda are coming to Stone Wall . . . tomorrow! Am I dreaming?

7
00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:44.598
I wish Gliss and Darb were coming too. But that's okay.

8
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.150
Maybe I can meet them another time."

9
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:52.230
Loro scratched his head. "I still don't understand why they're coming here.

10
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:57.709
Maybe you should send another message and remind them that we don't know if that was a relic that we saw.

11
00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.970
We don't even know if the cave is anything special."

12
00:01:02.216 --> 00:01:05.934
Raff shrugged. "You could be right, Loro.

13
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:11.790
But they know more about relics than we do, and the crown and staff do seem old and valuable.

14
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:14.810
It's probably a good idea for them to come."

15
00:01:14.972 --> 00:01:21.179
Loro didn't look convinced. "To me, it seems like a waste of time.

16
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.221
Who knows if any of that stuff actually belonged to King Zanta."

17
00:01:26.222 --> 00:01:29.055
"I have my doubts too," Raff said.

18
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:34.030
"But we are very close to Zanta's fortress—it's only a couple of zaps away.

19
00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.450
We've been there on school field trips a couple of times."

20
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.590
"Really?" Now Loro looked interested. "That's cool."

21
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.429
Zella didn't seem to be listening to the conversation at all.

22
00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:49.710
"I can't wait to ask Zann and Perda about their adventures.

23
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.589
I mean, I read or watched all their interviews.

24
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:56.370
But I have so many questions for them."

25
00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:02.137
"They're not coming here to answer their number one fan's questions," Raff said.

26
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.096
He thought about what Zann and Perda had revealed in their message.

27
00:02:06.097 --> 00:02:10.400
"I remember reading about those shape-shifters from Fest.

28
00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.390
But I don't understand why they would be here in Magica.

29
00:02:13.894 --> 00:02:17.262
Or why they'd be interested in the Mask of Zanta.

30
00:02:17.263 --> 00:02:20.204
Zella, can I borrow those books again when we get home?"

31
00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:25.467
"Sure," Zella said. "I'm curious about the Festians too.

32
00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.570
Let's forget about sneaking into the cave for now.

33
00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.350
We can go home and get the books and read about Fest."

34
00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.810
"I doubt you'll learn anything," Loro said.

35
00:02:34.972 --> 00:02:40.847
Raff shrugged. "We might. Besides, we need to check on Muncher too.

36
00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.890
It's weird how he acted earlier."

37
00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.430
They walked back toward the village.

38
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:51.570
Halfway there, they came across Muncher. He was in a clearing, nibbling at some flowers.

39
00:02:51.597 --> 00:02:57.554
"Huh, there you are." Raff patted the donkey. "Why did you run off?"

40
00:02:57.555 --> 00:03:01.012
"Hee-haw!" was the animal's only reply.

41
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.530
He trotted off toward home, and the three kids followed.

42
00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.490
When they reached the edge of the village, Raff and Zella turned in the direction of their house.

43
00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.589
But Loro stopped. "I should go home and check on my new house.

44
00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.710
My parents are away for a few days."

45
00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:22.310
"Your parents left already?" Raff was surprised.

46
00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:27.630
"But you just got here. Did they have to take care of something back at your old home?"

47
00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.269
"Something like that." Loro waved and took off.

48
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.910
"Good luck with your reading. See you later."

49
00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.150
Soon Raff and Zella were in her room, surrounded by books.

50
00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:43.209
Raff quickly found some information about Fest.

51
00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:47.009
He and Zella read it over several times.

52
00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.209
"It says that Fest doesn't have much natural magic," Zella said.

53
00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.770
"That's why Festians travel through the vortex more than most people.

54
00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.450
They like to visit other worlds so they can use their magic energy in those places."

55
00:03:59.677 --> 00:04:06.632
"Zann's parents say it's a confusing world to visit," Raff said, pointing to a different paragraph in the book.

56
00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.589
"The people can change how they look anytime they want.

57
00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.910
It's the only kind of magic that's easy for them in their home world."

58
00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.610
A few minutes later, Zella tossed the books aside and groaned.

59
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.990
"This isn't really telling us anything useful."

60
00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:27.069
They wandered back outside. They saw old Panno sitting on his usual bench.

61
00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.549
"Hey." Raff grabbed Zella's arm.

62
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.204
"I just thought of something. Panno came here from another world.

63
00:04:35.205 --> 00:04:40.137
That means he probably knows more about the vortex than anyone else in Stone Wall.

64
00:04:40.138 --> 00:04:43.012
Let's ask him if he knows anything about Fest."

65
00:04:43.013 --> 00:04:45.853
"Good idea," Zella said.

66
00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.340
The kids hurried over to the old man.

67
00:04:48.341 --> 00:04:54.114
"Hello, young ones," Panno said. He peered past them.

68
00:04:54.115 --> 00:04:56.804
"Where's your new friend?"

69
00:04:56.805 --> 00:05:01.596
"You mean Loro?" Zella shrugged. "He had to go home.

70
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.190
But we have a question for you.

71
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.170
Do you know anything about a world called Fest?

72
00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:11.490
Or why Festians might want to cause trouble here in Magica?"

73
00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:18.892
Old Panno narrowed his eyes. "I visited that place once when I was young."

74
00:05:18.893 --> 00:05:22.304
Raff and Zella looked at each other and grinned.

75
00:05:22.305 --> 00:05:25.229
"You mean Fest?" Raff asked.

76
00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:31.030
"You've actually been there?" Zella said eagerly. "What's it like?"

77
00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:35.981
"It was strange and disturbing," the old man said.

78
00:05:35.982 --> 00:05:43.387
"The people could look like anyone from a noseless Niffian to the queen of Magica.

79
00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:47.850
But I could never read what was truly in their hearts.

80
00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:56.330
I left there as quickly as I could because it was the only world where my magic failed me."

81
00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.870
He stood up slowly, leaning on his cane.

82
00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:08.489
"Although now that I'm so old, my magic fails me sometimes in Magica too."

83
00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:16.304
"Wait," Zella said. "Panno, do you know why Festians might come here and steal stuff? We think that . . ."

84
00:06:16.305 --> 00:06:23.512
Panno was hobbling away. "I have to go now." His voice sounded hoarse.

85
00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.609
Zella took a step after him.

86
00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:29.750
"Don't, Zella." Raff grabbed her arm to stop her.

87
00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:33.270
Old Panno seemed tired and disturbed by something.

88
00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:38.950
"Leave him alone. We can ask Zann and Perda about Fest when they get here."
